# LaTeX build intermediates. report.pdf IS committed -- it is the attachable artifact,
# and committing it means a reader gets the report without needing MiKTeX. The files below
# are regenerated by build.ps1 on every run and carry no information.
#
# report.tex and references.bib ARE committed: the .tex is the source the numeric audit
# (scripts/check_report_numbers.py) reads, and the .bib is the bibliography database that
# bibtex needs. Neither is an intermediate.
report.aux
report.log
report.out
report.toc
report.synctex.gz

# biblatex/biber intermediates. report.bbl is generated from references.bib on every
# build, so it is not a source either. report-blx.bib is biblatex's internal control file,
# written only under backend=bibtex -- the biber build does not produce it (verified by
# deleting it and rebuilding), but it is listed so a future backend switch cannot commit it.
report.bbl
report.blg
report.bcf
report.run.xml
report-blx.bib

# The journal manuscript template the report is typeset on, as supplied by the user on
# 2026-10-12. Deliberately NOT committed: it is a third-party document (the *Research
# Future* author template, placeholder authors and all), this repository is public, and
# its redistribution terms were never read -- the same caution this project applied to a
# corpus licence it could not authenticate. Nothing in the build reads it; report.tex is
# self-contained. Consequence, stated so nobody is surprised: a fresh clone will NOT have
# this file, so AGENTS.md's references to it describe a file on the author's disk, not a
# repository artifact. Committing it is the user's call, not an agent's.
new main.tex
